      "body": "Andrew and Nabil first met at an MRC CLIMB hackathon, where Andrew also learnt to play Pandemic. Further hackathons and conferences kept them in contact, and a Slack group grew out of one of those events. Lee joined that group early. His connection with Nabil also involved email correspondence about EnteroBase and CDC data submissions to the short read archive.\n\nThe three had already collaborated closely on a paper in 2017 before they had all met in person. That paper began with a Slack discussion comparing MLST software: which implementations worked, which did not, and how they performed against one another. Andrew recalls the work moving so quickly that CDC clearance struggled to keep pace. This experience showed how an informal conversation could become a useful shared resource."
