      "body": "The podcast was intended to preserve practical knowledge exchanged over coffee, at bars and in Slack discussions. The hosts describe information scattered across Reddit, Biostars and other sources, alongside insider knowledge that newcomers might otherwise acquire only after spending considerable time in the community.\n\nThey considered a blog or a small magazine-style PDF, but drafting written material felt too formal and labour-intensive. Andrew and Lee had also chaired virtual lab talks over Zoom, recording presentations for YouTube. Those talks were useful, but polished seminars did not reproduce the casual conversations they wanted to capture.\n\nThey deliberately chose a narrow microbial bioinformatics focus rather than covering all microbiology or bioinformatics. Read mapping, for example, means different things in different organisms. Lee cites How I Built This, Planet Money and Science Friday as influences; Nabil watches a lot of topic-led YouTube videos, which reassured him that anyone with something interesting to say will find an audience."
